## 7. WAFA CHARGELAB

Build ChargeLab as a complete battery and charging analytics subsystem.

### Live battery monitoring

Use supported Android battery broadcasts and BatteryManager APIs.

Read the following where available:

- Battery percentage
- Charging, discharging, full or not-charging state
- Plugged power source
- Battery temperature
- Battery voltage
- Current or charge-counter readings, when accessible
- Battery saver state
- Relevant battery status information

Use appropriate units and convert raw values only after verifying their documented units.

Show unavailable values explicitly. Do not substitute zero for missing measurements.

### Charging sessions

Automatically detect charging-state transitions while the application is active or monitoring is legitimately running.

Store:

- Session identifier
- Start and end timestamps
- Initial and final battery percentages
- Session duration
- Recorded battery temperature samples
- Available voltage and current samples
- Charging-source changes
- Charging interruptions
- Sampling gaps
- Session completion reason

Persist session data in Room.

Recover safely after process termination and distinguish a confirmed session end from an incomplete session.

### Charging analytics

Implement:

- Battery percentage timeline
- Percentage points gained per hour
- Charging duration statistics
- Session comparison
- Minimum and maximum recorded temperature
- Available voltage and current graphs
- Historical charging summaries
- Estimated time to a selected charge target

Time-to-target estimates must use recent observations, account for charging variability and display an uncertainty indication. Do not promise an exact completion time.

Do not calculate charging wattage unless reliable voltage and current measurements with appropriate units are available. If calculated, label the value as an estimate and explain the measurement limitations.

### Battery health

Show battery health indicators only when the device exposes trustworthy information.

Do not invent:

- Battery health percentages
- Battery cycle counts
- Original battery capacity
- Actual remaining battery capacity
- Battery replacement recommendations based solely on battery percentage

If the operating system does not expose a value, explain the limitation.

### Charging alerts

Provide optional user-configured alerts for:

- Selected battery percentage
- Available temperature readings crossing a configurable threshold
- Charging interruption
- Unexpectedly long charging sessions, where sufficient evidence exists

Use local notifications and request notification permission when required.

Never automatically enable charging alerts without informing the user.

